rror_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20454, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01KnAtWmdE1FnRK3Po53yPHp", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20454, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01HRKCjL4UdAHWgzRpCytPaw", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20754, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01HRKCjL4UdAHWgzRpCytPaw", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20754, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01HRKCjL4UdAHWgzRpCytPaw", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25392, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01PY9JxP1YMEnTTJQkGW3SCm", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed, it failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial_failure), which left the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt finished the rollout. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging) and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55992, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01PY9JxP1YMEnTTJQkGW3SCm", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55992, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01PY9JxP1YMEnTTJQkGW3SCm", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 57830, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_0166adU9ybAGY3poRcSuSbdE", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58130, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_0166adU9ybAGY3poRcSuSbdE", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58130, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_0166adU9ybAGY3poRcSuSbdE", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 62869, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001. The service is healthy again and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The bad v2.3.1 had also failed in staging as v2.3.1-rc. The first rollback stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, so for a while us-east was on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. I ran the same rollback again and it finished. All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) now run v2.3.0. No approval was needed because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Checking the incident list showed it had gone through anyway, so I didn't send it again and only one on-call page went out. The incident describes the outage, the stalled first rollback and the fix. It lists two follow-ups: finding why v2.3.1 failed and looking into the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BqYYzFLsPDWfq2Nz2K9NJL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01GJ7M4K4mSpiy3sa2cePpmT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01V8HNifDfwuJkEDp8hRfxzg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VmoWJfRUSCj4oDg7LhEpoE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped after us-east. Re-running a rollback to the same version is safe, so I'll try once more to finish the other regions.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012etJBFw5JPQLci4fQr2BBg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01KnAtWmdE1FnRK3Po53yPHp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HRKCjL4UdAHWgzRpCytPaw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PY9JxP1YMEnTTJQkGW3SCm", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed, it failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), with an error rate of about 18%. We rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial_failure), which left the regions on mixed versions. A second attempt finished the rollout. All regions now run v2.3.0, the service is healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging) and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0166adU9ybAGY3poRcSuSbdE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001. The service is healthy again and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The bad v2.3.1 had also failed in staging as v2.3.1-rc. The first rollback stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, so for a while us-east was on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west were still on v2.3.1. I ran the same rollback again and it finished. All three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) now run v2.3.0. No approval was needed because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Checking the incident list showed it had gone through anyway, so I didn't send it again and only one on-call page went out. The incident describes the outage, the stalled first rollback and the fix. It lists two follow-ups: finding why v2.3.1 failed and looking into the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}